--TEST--
A `private` property and a `private` method are both refused where they are read from another class — `rule:core-api/written-visibility`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The level is a fact about *where the code is written*, so a receiver typed
// as `Vault` buys nothing: the same two references would be legal inside
// `Vault`'s own bodies and are refused here, one diagnostic each, from the
// one run.
class Vault {
    private int $balance = 0;
    private function audit(): int { return $this->balance; }
    public function total(): int { return $this->balance; }
}
class Thief {
    public function take(Vault $v): int {
        int $seen = $v->balance;
        return $seen + $v->audit();
    }
}
echo "never reached", "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0471]: `Vault::$balance` is `private`, so only `Vault`'s own bodies reach it
%A
error[E0471]: `Vault::audit()` is `private`, so only `Vault`'s own bodies reach it
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
